{"nodes": [{"id": "test_result_testing_protocol", "label": "Main/Testing Agent Communication Protocol", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "test_result.md", "source_location": "lines 1-97", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "test_result.md is the single YAML-structured channel between the main agent and the testing agent, holding complete testing state and history. The main agent must update it (status_history, needs_retesting, test_plan, agent_communication) BEFORE invoking the testing agent, since the testing agent reads it to know what to test. stuck_count tracks repeat failures and is only reset once the testing agent confirms a fix \u2014 preventing premature declarations of success."}, {"id": "test_result_resume_parser_pdfparse_bug", "label": "pdf-parse Import Bug (Resume Parser)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "test_result.md", "source_location": "lines 145-159, 275-281", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CRITICAL bug: resume parsing threw 'pdfParse.default is not a function' at resume-parser.service.ts:45 because pdf-parse v2.4.5 was imported as '* as pdfParse' and called via (pdfParse as any).default(buffer). Fixed by switching to a default import and calling pdfParse(buffer). Blocked all resume upload functionality; stuck_count 1, still marked needs_retesting."}, {"id": "test_result_anti_scraping_blockage", "label": "Job Board Anti-Scraping Blockage", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "test_result.md", "source_location": "lines 161-189, 290-299", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Indeed returns 403 Forbidden and LinkedIn is likewise blocked, so scraping returns 0 jobs even though the endpoints, error handling and DB integration work. Treated as expected behavior and documented in code; the testing agent's recommendation is to use official job board APIs instead of scraping for production."}, {"id": "test_result_backend_test_sequence_1", "label": "Backend Test Sequence 1 Results", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "test_result.md", "source_location": "lines 266-299", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "7 backend services tested, 6 passing (85.7%). Passing: AI Service Integration, Indeed scraper, LinkedIn scraper, Job Matching, Application Agent, Authentication. Failing: Resume Parser (pdf-parse import). Email verification requires SMTP and was worked around for testing."}, {"id": "test_result_emergent_llm_key", "label": "Emergent LLM Key Configuration", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "test_result.md", "source_location": "lines 136-141, 262", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "AI service runs on OpenAI GPT-4 via a single Emergent LLM key (a universal key spanning OpenAI/Anthropic/Google), verified as initializing the OpenAI client correctly. Note the key value is committed in plain text in test_result.md, contradicting the API key management policy in AI_SERVICES_GUIDE.md."}, {"id": "test_result_about_page_task", "label": "About Page (Figma-derived)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "test_result.md", "source_location": "lines 113-127, 222-232", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "About page converted from Figma CSS to Tailwind at frontend/src/pages/about.js with hero, features and community sections. Initial breakage was an import error \u2014 Navbar and Footer are named exports, not default exports."}, {"id": "test_result_user_problem_statement", "label": "Jobocate Enhancement Problem Statement", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "test_result.md", "source_location": "lines 105-111", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Four goals: (1) About page matching Figma, (2) AI-powered resume processing that parses PDFs and auto-populates profiles, (3) job aggregation and matching from LinkedIn and Indeed, (4) user-driven application process where users mark jobs interested and an agent handles applications."}], "edges": [{"source": "test_result_backend_test_sequence_1", "target": "test_result_resume_parser_pdfparse_bug", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "test_result.md", "source_location": "lines 275-281", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "test_result_backend_test_sequence_1", "target": "test_result_anti_scraping_blockage", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "test_result.md", "source_location": "lines 290-293", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "test_result_backend_test_sequence_1", "target": "test_result_emergent_llm_key", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "test_result.md", "source_location": "line 283", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "test_result_backend_test_sequence_1", "target": "test_result_testing_protocol", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "test_result.md", "source_location": "lines 1-97, 266-299", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "test_result_resume_parser_pdfparse_bug", "target": "phase1_implementation_resume_parser_module", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "test_result.md", "source_location": "lines 145-159", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "test_result_resume_parser_pdfparse_bug", "target": "phase1_implementation_dependencies", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "test_result.md", "source_location": "lines 156-159", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "test_result_anti_scraping_blockage", "target": "phase1_implementation_job_scraper_module", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_fil